  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan", "title": "Guard",
      "items": [
        "Asks before a costly cold send, once per cold episode: Send anyway, or Don't send (hold, 0 AI credits)",
        "No answer in 5 minutes holds the send. A host that cannot ask gets the old refuse-once message",
        "Slash commands and ! shell escapes are never guarded; a running turn only gets the price note",
        "refused.json lets the next send, even from a new process, through"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald", "title": "Clock",
      "items": [
        "TTL, expiry and prices come from assistant.usage; nothing is guessed",
        "assistant.usage is not replayed on resume, so events.jsonl seeds the clock",
        "Heads-up leads by the smaller of the setting and a fifth of the TTL, never mid-turn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet", "title": "VS Code, measured 11-12 Oct 2026",
      "items": [
        "Extension loads only with chat.canvases.enabled, from a project install (.github/extensions)",
        "Cards, help and settings show as a question with OK; the heads-up and sending-cold note reach only VS Code's log",
        "Sessions keep usage checkpoints only, so the report counts them as totals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber", "title": "Limits",
      "items": [
        "Reported expiry is an upper bound: Luna was served cold at 29 of 30 minutes",
        "/cache-clock works typed in full in VS Code but is not in its / menu",
        "No keep-warm pings yet"
      ]
    }
  ]
